⏺ Let me look at the current file to confirm context.

  Read 1 file (ctrl+o to expand)

⏺ The logic is correct: it retries up to attempts times, backs off exponentially between attempts (skipping the wait
  after the final failure), and rethrows the last error if all attempts fail.

  One edge case worth flagging: if attempts is 0 (or negative), lastError stays undefined and the function throws
  undefined instead of a real Error. This isn't a bug introduced by this diff's core logic, but since attempts now has a
  default and can be overridden by callers, it's worth guarding against (e.g. throw a descriptive error if attempts <
  1, or fall back to the old behavior of just calling fn() once).

  No other correctness issues — backoff math (delayMs * 2 ** i), the await on fn() so errors are caught, and the "don't
  wait after last attempt" condition are all correct.

  VERDICT: APPROVE

